EXT. BACKYARD - TENT - NIGHT

A small green tent lit from inside by a flashlight. Crickets. A sprinkler ticks in the neighbor's yard.

INT. TENT - CONTINUOUS

ROZ ABERNATHY, 38, in a bathrobe over scrubs, sits cross-legged on a sleeping bag. Across from her, MILO ABERNATHY, 8, holds a flashlight under his chin. A cell phone leans against a thermos between them, on speaker.

MILO
Are you sure he can hear us?

ROZ
He can hear us.

CALVIN (V.O.)
(over phone, crackling)
I can hear you, buddy. The connection's only a little bit bad.

MILO
Dad, it's cold in the tent.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Is it? Over here it's so hot I could fry an egg on my helmet.

ROZ
Calvin.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Sorry. Lieutenant's rules. No jokes about eggs.

MILO
Dad, when are you coming home?

CALVIN (V.O.)
Three more weeks, kiddo. Maybe less.

MILO
Mom said it was five.

ROZ
I said around five.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Your mom's a lawyer about it. She's always right.

ROZ
I'm a nurse.

CALVIN (V.O.)
That too.

MILO
Dad, do you see the same moon?

CALVIN (V.O.)
I think so. Is it the one with the face?

MILO
It's the one with the face.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Then I see it. I'm looking right at it.

ROZ
Milo, tell Dad what you did at school.

MILO
I got a sticker for reading out loud.

CALVIN (V.O.)
What book?

MILO
The one about the bear who can't sleep.

CALVIN (V.O.)
I love that one. Did you do the bear voice?

MILO
(low growl)
Grrr, I can't sleep.

CALVIN (V.O.)
That's perfect. That's the best bear I ever heard.

ROZ
It's a quarter to ten, baby.

MILO
Five more minutes.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Listen to your mom.

MILO
Okay. Goodnight, Dad.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Goodnight, Milo. Tell the moon I said hello.

MILO
I will.

ROZ
Goodnight, Calvin.

CALVIN (V.O.)
Love you both.

ROZ
Love you.

MILO
Love you.

The line clicks. The flashlight flickers and goes out.
